# round-45 figure ledger DRAFT (ExecFiguresLedger) — NOT a landed ledger.
# Grammar observed in .ufo/waves/round-45/count-c1.py (parse_ledger/parse_pipeline):
#   id <TAB> value <TAB> class <TAB> command          (4 cells, MOVE rows)
#   id <TAB> value <TAB> class <TAB> command <TAB> CONST=<reason>   (5 cells, revision-constant rows)
# `?` in the value cell = deliberately unasserted. The L1 re-measures at the landed tip and
# writes the integer into cell 2. Nothing else needs editing: CONST rows already carry their
# fifth cell; MOVE rows are 4 cells and must differ between --rev and --other-rev.
# Every command is one git pipeline naming @REV@, runs under the counter's no-shell tokenizer
# (FILTERS = grep/head/tail/wc/sort/uniq/cut/tr/cat/nl), and prints one integer.
# Expected landed values and entering-tip measurements: .ufo/waves/round-45/w1/ExecFiguresLedger.md
F01	?	registry	git show @REV@:corpus/SOURCES.md | grep -cE '^ {0,3}\|[[:space:]]*S[0-9]{3,}'
F02	?	corpus	git ls-tree -r --name-only @REV@ corpus/lessons | grep -c '\.md$'
F03	?	corpus	git ls-tree -r --name-only @REV@ corpus/knowledge | grep -c '\.md$'
F04	?	checks	git ls-tree -r --name-only @REV@ tools | grep -cE '\.(py|sh)$'	CONST=round-45 plan rewrites tools/mori-gate-registry.py and edits three existing tools; it adds no tools/ filename
F05	?	registry	git show @REV@:SKILL.md | grep -cE '^\| [^|]+ \| (gate|probe)'
F06	?	registry	git show @REV@:SKILL.md | grep -cE '^\| name \| kind \| entry \| verdict map \| self-test \| pinned values \| write scope \| owner \|$'	CONST=the round adds rows to existing eight-cell tables, never a new table header
F07	?	evidence	git show @REV@:.ufo/waves/round-44/w1/ExecGateInventory.md | grep -c 'unregistered: no row names'	CONST=round 44 is admitted and its inventory bytes are closed
F08	?	checks	git grep -n -- '--selftest' @REV@ -- tools | grep -vE ':[0-9]+:[[:space:]]*#' | cut -d: -f2 | sort -u | grep -cE '\.(py|sh)$'
F09	?	checks	git show @REV@:.ufo/waves/round-44/count-c1.py | wc -l	CONST=round-44 counter bytes closed at round-44 admission
F10	?	checks	git show @REV@:.ufo/waves/round-44/count-c2.py | wc -l	CONST=round-44 counter bytes closed at round-44 admission
F11	?	checks	git show @REV@:.ufo/waves/round-44/count-c3.py | wc -l	CONST=round-44 counter bytes closed at round-44 admission
F12	?	wave	git ls-tree -r --name-only @REV@ .ufo/waves/round-43/w1 | grep -c '\.md$'	CONST=round 43 is closed; its w1 report set cannot grow
F13	?	wave	git ls-tree -r --name-only @REV@ .ufo/waves/round-44/w1 | grep -c '\.md$'	CONST=round 44 is closed; its w1 report set cannot grow
F14	?	evidence	git show @REV@:.ufo/waves/round-43/logs/residual8/ResCritBulkAppend.log | grep -oE '\b[EW][0-9]{2}\b' | sort -u | wc -l	CONST=round-43 log bytes are closed; it is the lane's only committed copy of the sources-census code space
F15	?	evidence	git show @REV@:.ufo/waves/round-44/evidence/census-end.txt | grep -oE '^rows=[0-9]+' | cut -d= -f2	CONST=round-44 census receipt is closed
# MOVE rows and their expected landed values (entering-tip values on the line above each id in
# the report's catalogue): F01=246 (+1 C3 entry) · F02=75 (73 @554ff416, 74 @3ad8faaa, +1
# round-45 lesson) · F03=55 (+1 C3 knowledge entry) · F05=50 (+3 orphan-tool rows, +3 round-45
# counter rows, +1 append-only superseding row) · F08=31 (+3 tools given a real --selftest branch).
